**Location:** `ActionButtons` → `triggerActionItemsGeneration`, line ~471

```kotlin
scope.launch {
    kotlinx.coroutines.delay(3000)   // ← blind wait, not data-driven
    triggerActionItemsGeneration(context)
}
```

Four WebViews are triggered to refresh, then Claude is called after a hardcoded 3-second wait hoping data has arrived. If the network is slow, Claude receives stale/null data; if fast, 3 seconds is wasted.

**Fix — count completions before calling Claude:**

```kotlin
// Replace the delay + trigger pattern with a counter in ScrapeBridge
private var pendingRefreshCount = AtomicInteger(0)
private var onAllRefreshed: (() -> Unit)? = null

class ScrapeBridge {
    @JavascriptInterface
    fun reportData(json: String) {
        Handler(Looper.getMainLooper()).post {
            // existing parse logic ...
            if (pendingRefreshCount.decrementAndGet() == 0) {
                onAllRefreshed?.invoke()
                onAllRefreshed = null
            }
        }
    }
}

// In ActionButtons onClick:
pendingRefreshCount.set(SOURCES.size)
onAllRefreshed = { scope.launch { triggerActionItemsGeneration(context) } }
SOURCES.forEach { src -> webViewMap[src.name]?.evaluateJavascript("if (window.refresh) window.refresh();", null) }
```

---

**Location:** `DashboardScreen`, lines 521–527

```kotlin
val myAvail by myAvailState          // recomposes on ANY state change
val outlookPersonal by outlookPersonalState
val outlookDboOps by outlookDboOpsState
val planner by plannerState
val items by actionItemsState
val loading by actionItemsLoading
val error by actionItemsError
```

Every tile (`InboxTile`, `ActivitiesTile`, etc.) recomposes whenever **any** of these global states change — even if only `plannerState` updated, `InboxTile` still recomposes.

**Fix — push state reads down into each tile:**

```kotlin
@Composable
fun InboxTile() {
    val personal by outlookPersonalState  // only recomposes when this changes
    val dboOps by outlookDboOpsState
    TileCard(title = "Inbox") { /* ... */ }
}

@Composable
fun DashboardScreen(modifier: Modifier = Modifier) {
    // No state reads here — just compose the tiles
    Column(modifier = modifier.verticalScroll(rememberScrollState()).padding(8.dp), ...) {
        ActionItemsTile(onGenerate = { scope.launch { triggerActionItemsGeneration(context) } })
        InboxTile()
        ActivitiesTile()
        PlannerTile()
        MessagesTile()
    }
}
```

